ance, and table-wide apply time is not a valid substitute."},{"id":"existing-owner-write-evidence","statement":"Owner-write chronology must derive from the existing cache-only row HLC and its physical component; do not add durable nodes columns, invent a commit timestamp, or claim pre-dispatch producer attribution that the canonical owner currently rebases away."},{"id":"production-seam-replay","statement":"The deterministic discriminator must exercise the real heartbeat intent, canonical node-state publication owner, CDC event/cache ingress, snapshot owner, and MovieLens schema-admission report path; stubs may observe outer effects but cannot replace the binding owner seams."},{"id":"negative-control-matrix","statement":"Missing heartbeat publication, delayed canonical write, delayed CDC observation, expired or missing lease, causally older CDC replay, authoritative cache replacement, unexpired lease, and inactive terminal-node controls must remain independently distinguishable and cannot make a stale snapshot fresh."},{"id":"stable-report-vocabulary","statement":"The structured witness may be retained in snapshots and reports, but time-varying witness values must not be embedded in reason codes, error strings, transition keys, or metric identities."},{"id":"live-last","statement":"Do not rerun the unchanged MovieLens scenario. A single changed-source production run is allowed only after three deterministic scenario passes, red-on-revert evidence, exact independent verification, clean-container and source-fingerprint preflight, and a cool host; its purpose is attribution rather than weakening or relabeling the sealed gate."}],"frontierIds":["movielens-ready-lease-chronology-discriminator-main"]}}
